{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f6924c17-9daf-4270-b9c3-68e8f37b8c8a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8301742c744dd31a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9004-49kcszeh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9004-E001.md","content":"# Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode — documentation authoring\n\n## Description\n\nAuthor and publish a disconnected-environment install guide for KServe raw\ndeployment mode in the product documentation. The capability already exists and\nworks in the product; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams\ncurrently rediscover the required steps — which images to mirror, which\noperators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install — from private gists and\nfield enablement material. This epic converts that existing source material\ninto maintained product documentation.\n\nNo product behavior changes: no code, operator, or default-configuration\nchanges are in scope. Serverless-mode disconnected support is explicitly out of\nscope.\n\n## Scope\n\nAuthor a single disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode,\nstructured as follows (content outline):\n\n1. **Prerequisites** — requirements for a disconnected cluster targeting raw\n   deployment mode, including the mirror registry setup needed before install.\n2. **Operator configuration** — which operators to install and which to skip\n   for raw deployment mode in a disconnected environment (the mode uses plain\n   Deployments/Services with no mesh dependency, so serverless-only operators\n   are skipped).\n3. **Image-mirroring reference** — the complete list of required images for a\n   disconnected install, and the procedure for deriving the digest list per\n   release.\n4. **Validation steps** — how to verify a successful air-gapped install of\n   KServe raw deployment mode.\n5. **Troubleshooting** — a section covering the three most common\n   field-reported failure modes: image pull errors, missing runtime, and\n   storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n\nSource material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and\ntechnical review work, not research.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** a disconnected cluster, **when** a user follows the published\n  guide, **then** they can complete a KServe raw deployment mode install\n  (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation) — measured by the guide\n  existing in the product documentation with all three sections present and\n  technically reviewed. (HLR-1)\n- **Given** the guide, **when** a user prepares their mirror registry,\n  **then** it contains a complete image-mirroring reference listing the\n  required images and documenting how to derive the digest list per release —\n  measured by technical review confirming the image list matches the shipped\n  release. (HLR-2)\n- **Given** the guide, **when** a user hits one of the three most common\n  field-reported failure modes (image pull errors, missing runtime,\n  storage-initializer misconfiguration), **then** the troubleshooting section\n  covers it — measured by the section covering all three named failure modes.\n  (HLR-3)\n- **Accuracy validation (mandatory):** the guide's claims about KServe raw\n  deployment mode are validated against the platform architecture context —\n  in particular that raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh\n  dependency) is the recommended path for disconnected environments, that\n  Service Mesh / Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies,\n  and that Serving Runtimes provide model execution. The guide must not\n  contradict the architecture context.\n- **Technical review:** the published guide is technically reviewed against\n  the actual implementation by the KServe owning team before publication.\n- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes are introduced by this\n  work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | Disconnected install guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — fully covered |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Image-mirroring reference (required images, per-release digest derivation) — fully covered |\n| HLR-3 | P2 | Troubleshooting section for the three named failure modes — fully covered |\n\nAll three HLRs are covered by this single epic; the strategy was triaged as\ndocumentation-only, so no priority-based split is applied.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":21819,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96fa705d47b24307","agent_id":"a1e0466b1c658f4b9","session_id":"6da44e59-e9c0-4193-8ee6-80f8069cb51f","uuid":"cebd5035-dad7-42d7-a78b-619f88cc4cd3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:49:34.379Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9004 strategy"}
