{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bf97e00efc77fbf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode — documentation authoring\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAuthor and publish a disconnected-environment install guide for KServe raw\n34\tdeployment mode in the product documentation. The capability already exists and\n35\tworks in the product; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams\n36\tcurrently rediscover the required steps — which images to mirror, which\n37\toperators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install — from private gists and\n38\tfield enablement material. This epic converts that existing source material\n39\tinto maintained product documentation.\n40\t\n41\tNo product behavior changes: no code, operator, or default-configuration\n42\tchanges are in scope. Serverless-mode disconnected support is explicitly out of\n43\tscope.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\tAuthor a single disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode,\n48\tstructured as follows (content outline):\n49\t\n50\t1. **Prerequisites** — requirements for a disconnected cluster targeting raw\n51\t   deployment mode, including the mirror registry setup needed before install.\n52\t2. **Operator configuration** — which operators to install and which to skip\n53\t   for raw deployment mode in a disconnected environment (the mode uses plain\n54\t   Deployments/Services with no mesh dependency, so serverless-only operators\n55\t   are skipped).\n56\t3. **Image-mirroring reference** — the complete list of required images for a\n57\t   disconnected install, and the procedure for deriving the digest list per\n58\t   release.\n59\t4. **Validation steps** — how to verify a successful air-gapped install of\n60\t   KServe raw deployment mode.\n61\t5. **Troubleshooting** — a section covering the three most common\n62\t   field-reported failure modes: image pull errors, missing runtime, and\n63\t   storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n64\t\n65\tSource material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and\n66\ttechnical review work, not research.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- **Given** a disconnected cluster, **when** a user follows the published\n71\t  guide, **then** they can complete a KServe raw deployment mode install\n72\t  (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation) — measured by the guide\n73\t  existing in the product documentation with all three sections present and\n74\t  technically reviewed. (HLR-1)\n75\t- **Given** the guide, **when** a user prepares their mirror registry,\n76\t  **then** it contains a complete image-mirroring reference listing the\n77\t  required images and documenting how to derive the digest list per release —\n78\t  measured by technical review confirming the image list matches the shipped\n79\t  release. (HLR-2)\n80\t- **Given** the guide, **when** a user hits one of the three most common\n81\t  field-reported failure modes (image pull errors, missing runtime,\n82\t  storage-initializer misconfiguration), **then** the troubleshooting section\n83\t  covers it — measured by the section covering all three named failure modes.\n84\t  (HLR-3)\n85\t- **Accuracy validation (mandatory):** the guide's claims about KServe raw\n86\t  deployment mode are validated against the platform architecture context —\n87\t  in particular that raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh\n88\t  dependency) is the recommended path for disconnected environments, that\n89\t  Service Mesh / Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies,\n90\t  and that Serving Runtimes provide model execution. The guide must not\n91\t  contradict the architecture context.\n92\t- **Technical review:** the published guide is technically reviewed against\n93\t  the actual implementation by the KServe owning team before publication.\n94\t- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes are introduced by this\n95\t  work.\n96\t\n97\t## HLR Traceability\n98\t\n99\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n100\t|-----|----------|----------|\n101\t| HLR-1 | P1 | Disconnected install guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — fully covered |\n102\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Image-mirroring reference (required images, per-release digest derivation) — fully covered |\n103\t| HLR-3 | P2 | Troubleshooting section for the three named failure modes — fully covered |\n104\t\n105\tAll three HLRs are covered by this single epic; the strategy was triaged as\n106\tdocumentation-only, so no priority-based split is applied.\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aadc9727cf7f182c","agent_id":"a3470bd6c98ea42b4","session_id":"6da44e59-e9c0-4193-8ee6-80f8069cb51f","uuid":"49c23e7d-57dd-4909-be3b-3c14357b77e4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:51:19.290Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bf97e00efc77fbf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
